A1. Those who do it last are English. ~ LAUGH
A6. You'll get a laugh out of this. ~ JUDGE
A11. In addition to. ~ ALSO
A12. The only thing under the sun some people get from a vacation. ~ TAN
A14. What makes the ocean salty. ~ SALT
A15. Something out there in the wide open spaces. ~ MAN
A16. What the bald-headed man said was cold in the restaurant. ~ COCOA
A18. What the goat said when Jonah told his fish story. ~ BAH
A19. Postscript (abr.). ~ PS
A20. Oatmeal. ~ HO
A21. Virginia (abr.) ~ VA
A23. A prefix. ~ DE
A24. The cat's. ~ MEOW
A26. Precious stones. ~ GEMS
A28. A musical note. ~ FA
A29. The only thing a woman won't use to win an argument. ~ LOGIC
A31. The initials of a famous American President. ~ TR
A33. The way a flapper tries to look on Fifth avenue. ~ PERT
A34. To disfigure. ~ MAR
A35. A well-known ending. ~ TAIL
A36. Doctor (abr.). ~ DR
A37. What you go under after the (nth) degree of Scotch. ~ TABLE
A39. Behold. ~ LO
A41. What the stocking manufacturer tells about his goods. ~ YARN
A43. A man of wisdom. ~ SAGE
A46. Otherwise. ~ OR
A48. What a little boy calls his mother. ~ MA
A50. Company (abr.). ~ CO
A51. To exist. ~ BE
A52. One thing to do to show a girl a good time. ~ KID
A54. The kind of a girl that men don't forget. ~ PEACH
A57. A bad actor. ~ HAM
A58. A famous garden. ~ EDEN
A60. How a lot of blonds get that way. ~ DYE
A61. A knight of the road. ~ HOBO
A62. What love does with a little gift of roses. ~ SENDS
A63. When to kiss a pretty girl. ~ OFTEN

D1. The only things that can get lit on wood alcohol and not suffer bad effects. ~ LAMPS
D2. Sorrowful exclamation. ~ ALAS
D3. United States Navy (abr.). ~ USN
D4. What will few second-hand cars do. ~ GO
D5. The name of a prize fighter who doesn't like fast blacks. ~ JACK
D7. We. ~ US
D8. The little thing that puts color in a girl's cheek. ~ DAB
D9. What you are when you're happy. ~ GLAD
D10. The only thing a lot of men would willingly give their mother-in-law. ~ ETHER
D12. A preposition. ~ TO
D13. What some girls say but don't mean when you ask for a kiss. ~ NO
D16. A good way to keep your head. ~ COOL
D17. With (fr.). ~ AVEC
D20. A masculine pronoun. ~ HE
D22. What Armour's claim their ham is. ~ AM
D24. What old maids never do. ~ MARRY
D25. A rag, a bone and a boyish bob. ~ WOMAN
D26. The reason men go to co-educational colleges. ~ GIRLS
D27. The way even the best line gets when it's overworked. ~ STALE
D28. What a chorus girl wants to be at night. ~ FED
D30. What they do at a tea party. ~ GAB
D32. River (Spanish). ~ RIO
D37. "Spring has come," said the mouse as he danced around in it. ~ TRAP
D38. Every. ~ EACH
D40. The proof that women can take them is that they marry. ~ JOKES
D42. Before noon. ~ AM
D44. What the irate father said to his prospective son-in-law as the clock struck twelve. ~ GO
D45. Something to squeeze. ~ LEMON
D47. What the Swedish girl took in a red automobile. ~ RIDE
D49. What a man does for his girl when they go to a show. ~ PAYS
D51. This is not a ruthless work, though it concerns baseball. ~ BABE
D53. A husband's retreat. ~ DEN
D55. The way only a few address the Prince of Wales. ~ ED
D56. A university degree. ~ CE
D57. A kind of dog. ~ HOT
D59. North Dakota (abr.). ~ ND
D61. High flyer (abr.). Damn clever these puzzle makers. ~ HF


